The SVG files in this directory are original geometric interface symbols:
a landscape block, a control panel, a signal lamp, an anvil and an experiment
flask. Their filenames identify the interface roles in which they are used.
They do not reproduce Minecraft textures or Forge / NeoForge project logos.

player-skin.svg is the original source for player-skin.png, a blue-violet
explorer character authored on a 64 x 64 skin atlas. It contains no pixels
from the Minecraft default skin. Both source and rendered PNG use MIT.

See the repository root LICENSE for the MIT license text. Minecraft, Forge
and NeoForge names identify their respective games or projects; their
trademarks remain with their owners. No endorsement is implied.

Regenerate the skin PNG with an SVG renderer, for example:
rsvg-convert --width 64 --height 64 --output player-skin.png player-skin.svg
